        "abstract": "The introductory part gives an historical review of light production and electrical illumination. In the first part the fundamentals of radiation are sketched with special regard to visible light and the spectral response of the eye is analysed taking into consideration both physical and physiological aspects. The essential properties of filament materials are discussed together with the methods employed for increasing the efficiency of incandescent lamps, such as gasfilling with argon or krypton and coiling or recoiling the filament. Lamp economics are explained on various graphs, showing the behaviour of incandescent lamps as the functions of impressed and design voltages.",
